# Settings for scripts/diagnose_google_groups.py.
#
# Copy this file to scripts/.env.google-groups (gitignored) and fill in the values from the client's
# Registry deployment, i.e. the same values the auth-server pod receives:
#   AWS:   the "Registry Secret" in AWS Secrets Manager (synced by External Secrets Operator)
#   Azure: the matching Key Vault secrets
# Or read them from the running pod: kubectl exec <auth-server-pod> -- printenv GOOGLE_ALLOWED_HD
#
# The service account key is a long-lived credential: don't paste it into chat or tickets, and delete
# your filled-in copy when you're done.

# The full service account key JSON, on one line, exactly as stored in the deployment's secret.
# Keep the "\n" sequences inside "private_key" as they are, and wrap the whole value in single quotes.
GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_KEY_JSON='{"type":"service_account","project_id":"...","private_key_id":"...","private_key":"<PEM key with \n line breaks>","client_email":"...@....iam.gserviceaccount.com","client_id":"...","token_uri":"https://oauth2.googleapis.com/token"}'

# The client's Google Workspace domain, e.g. vegogarden.com. Only groups at exactly
# <group>@<this domain> can grant Registry scopes.
GOOGLE_ALLOWED_HD=

# The client's Workspace customer ID (starts with "C"), as in GOOGLE_CUSTOMER_ID in the deployment's secret.
# Leave it commented out to find it: every successful lookup prints each group's "owner: customers/C…".
# GOOGLE_CUSTOMER_ID=
